      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T17:20:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I think I was right. Even if it gets called in multiple cpus, its called serially using `for_each_possible_cpu` and breaks out if any of the cpu call fails:\n```\n»       for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {\n»       »       if (cpu \u003d\u003d self)\n»       »       »       continue;\n \n»       »       /*\n»       »        * Second hypercall to switch the mmu and ept pgtable\n»       »        * for other cpus other than boot cpu.\n»       »        */\n»       »       ret \u003d smp_call_function_single(cpu, do_pkvm_finalise,\n»       »       »       »       »              NULL, true);\n»       »       if (ret) {\n»       »       »       pr_err(\"%s: pkvm finalise on cpu: %d failed!\\n\",\n»       »       »       »       »       __func__, cpu);\n»       »       »       goto out;\n»       »       }\n»       }\n```\n\nSo if one cpu fails, we revert all cpus to privileged and return ret. I think this implementation is correct",
      "parentUuid": "0ee19699_57e65ee8",
      "revId": "1bbc05126ceb9a984a054529f255bc6fcd6be8b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
